IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mtpd-dates`

-- Medical Treatment Planning and Decisions Act 2016 (Vic) -- the rules a person meets about their own medical treatment
-- when they may lose, or have lost, the capacity to decide: decision-making capacity (s 4), advance care directives
-- (Part 2), appointed medical treatment decision makers and support persons (Part 3), who decides and what may be done
-- to the person who cannot decide (Part 4), medical research procedures (Part 5, the consent gate), VCAT rehearings
-- (s 88), health information (s 94), interstate instruments (ss 95-97), and the offences that protect the person.
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in mtpd-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, an "if",
-- "only if" or "unless" condition that fails, "must not", "is not permitted", "does not take effect ... unless", "is void",
-- a period the Act fixes); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment.
-- Questions with more than two answers return a choice whose "not covered" constructors play the part of NOTHING.
-- Judgments the Act leaves to someone else (a practitioner's reasonable belief, VCAT's satisfaction or order, the Public
-- Advocate's opinion) are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them. Forks (Fn) are listed in
-- NOTES.md.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Medical
-- Treatment Planning and Decisions Act 2016, Version No. 012 (1 July 2024), not the authorised version. (c) State of
-- Victoria; published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced
-- except in accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026
-- (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Medical Treatment Planning and Decisions Act 2016 -- the rules for the person whose treatment it is`

§§ `Part 1 -- definitions (s 3) and decision-making capacity (s 4)`

-- s 3(1): "adult means a person of or above the age of 18 years"; "child means a person under the age of 18 years".
GIVEN `the age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- an adult` `the age in years` IF `the age in years` AT LEAST 18

-- s 3(1): "significant treatment means any medical treatment of a person that involves any of the following -- (a) a
-- significant degree of bodily intrusion; (b) a significant risk to the person; (c) significant side effects;
-- (d) significant distress to the person"; "routine treatment means any medical treatment other than significant
-- treatment". Each limb is a judgment about the treatment, asked as a fact.
GIVEN `significant bodily intrusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `significant risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `significant side effects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `significant distress` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- significant treatment` `significant bodily intrusion` `significant risk` `significant side effects` `significant distress` IF
       `significant bodily intrusion`
    OR `significant risk`
    OR `significant side effects`
    OR `significant distress`

-- s 4(1): "A person has decision-making capacity to make a decision to which this Act applies if the person is able to do
-- the following -- (a) understand the information relevant to the decision and the effect of the decision; (b) retain
-- that information to the extent necessary to make the decision; (c) use or weigh that information as part of the
-- process of making the decision; (d) communicate the decision ... in some way". (2): "an adult is presumed to have
-- decision-making capacity unless there is evidence to the contrary". (4)(d): "a person has decision-making capacity to
-- make a decision if it is possible for the person to make a decision with practicable and appropriate support" -- so each
-- ability is asked "with any practicable and appropriate support". (4)(c): appearance and an unwise decision are not
-- grounds; they are not inputs. A child has no presumption: the four abilities decide.
DECLARE `Whether I have decision-making capacity` IS ONE OF
    `yes: as an adult I am presumed to have it, and there is no evidence to the contrary (s 4(2))`
    `yes: I can understand, retain, use and weigh, and communicate, with any practicable and appropriate support (s 4(1), (4)(d))`
    `no: I cannot do all four things s 4(1) asks, even with practicable and appropriate support`

GIVEN `the age in years` IS A NUMBER
      `there is evidence I may lack capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can understand the information and the effect of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can retain the information as far as needed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can use or weigh the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can communicate the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether I have decision-making capacity`
`s 4 -- my decision-making capacity` `the age in years` `there is evidence I may lack capacity` `I can understand the information and the effect of the decision` `I can retain the information as far as needed` `I can use or weigh the information` `I can communicate the decision` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `s 3 -- an adult` `the age in years` AND (NOT `there is evidence I may lack capacity`)
           THEN `yes: as an adult I am presumed to have it, and there is no evidence to the contrary (s 4(2))`
           IF     `I can understand the information and the effect of the decision`
              AND `I can retain the information as far as needed`
              AND `I can use or weigh the information`
              AND `I can communicate the decision`
           THEN `yes: I can understand, retain, use and weigh, and communicate, with any practicable and appropriate support (s 4(1), (4)(d))`
           OTHERWISE `no: I cannot do all four things s 4(1) asks, even with practicable and appropriate support`

§§ `Part 1 -- who may apply to VCAT (s 3, eligible applicant; ss 5, 22, 43, 65)`

DECLARE `Who is applying` IS ONE OF
    `me, the person whose treatment, directive or appointment it is`
    `a health practitioner who has my care or is treating me`
    `my medical treatment decision maker`
    `my support person`
    `the Public Advocate`
    `someone VCAT is satisfied has a special interest in my affairs`
    `anyone else (a relative or friend VCAT has not found to have a special interest)`

-- s 3(1): "eligible applicant means any of the following -- (a) a health practitioner who has the care of, or is providing
-- medical treatment to, a person; (b) the medical treatment decision maker of a person; (c) a person's support person;
-- (d) the Public Advocate; (e) any other person whom VCAT is satisfied has a special interest in the affairs of the person
-- concerned". A "means" definition: JUST FALSE outside it. The person concerned is not on the list (finding 3); they can
-- come in under (e) if VCAT is satisfied, and they are a party to the proceeding (ss 24, 47, 71).
GIVEN `the applicant` IS A `Who is applying`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- an eligible applicant` `the applicant` MEANS
    IF    `the applicant` EQUALS `me, the person whose treatment, directive or appointment it is`
       OR `the applicant` EQUALS `anyone else (a relative or friend VCAT has not found to have a special interest)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 2 -- giving an advance care directive (ss 13, 14, 16, 17, 21, 22)`

DECLARE `Who signed the document` IS ONE OF
    `I signed it myself`
    `an adult who is not a witness signed it at my direction`
    `someone else signed it at my direction (a child, a witness, or for an appointment an appointee)`
    `nobody signed it`

DECLARE `VCAT order on validity` IS ONE OF
    `no VCAT order about its validity`
    `VCAT declared it valid despite a failure to comply`
    `VCAT declared it invalid`

DECLARE `Whether my advance care directive is valid` IS ONE OF
    `void: I was induced to give it by dishonesty or undue influence (s 14(2))`
    `invalid: VCAT declared it invalid (s 22(2)(b)(i))`
    `valid: it came into force when it was signed (ss 13, 16, 17, 19(1))`
    `valid: VCAT declared it valid despite a failure to comply (s 22(2)(b)(ii))`
    `no effect as a directive: I lacked capacity for, or did not understand, a statement in it (s 13(a), s 21(1))`
    `no effect as a directive: it is not in writing in English with my full name, date of birth and address (s 16(1)(a), (b), s 21(1))`
    `no effect as a directive: it was not properly signed (s 16(1)(c), (2), s 21(1))`
    `no effect as a directive: the witnessing did not meet s 17(1) (s 21(1))`
    `no effect as a directive: the witnesses did not certify as s 17(2) and (3) require (s 21(1))`

-- s 13: "Any person (including a child) may give an advance care directive if -- (a) the person -- (i) has
-- decision-making capacity in relation to each statement in the directive; and (ii) understands the nature and effect of
-- each statement in the directive; and (b) the requirements of this Part are complied with."
-- s 16(1): "(a) must be in writing in English; and (b) must include the full name, date of birth and address of the
-- person giving it; and (c) subject to subsection (2), must be signed by the person giving it; and (d) must be witnessed
-- and certified in accordance with ... section 17." (2): another may sign at the person's direction if that signer "(a) is
-- an adult; and (b) is not a witness to the signing of the document".
-- s 17(1): "(a) 2 adult witnesses ...; (b) each witness must sign and date the document in the presence of -- (i) the
-- person giving the advance care directive; and (ii) each other; (c) at least one of the witnesses must be a registered
-- medical practitioner and must write the qualification ... on the document; (d) neither witness may be an appointed
-- medical treatment decision maker of the person ...; (e) in the case of an advance care directive being given by a
-- child, at least one of the witnesses must be a registered medical practitioner or psychologist with the prescribed
-- training and experience." The prescribed training is in regulations not deposited: asked as a fact.
-- s 17(2), (3): the certifications (apparent capacity, free and voluntary signing, signing in the presence of the two
-- witnesses, not an appointed decision maker, apparent understanding): one input.
-- s 14(2): "An advance care directive given in contravention of subsection (1) is void and of no effect."
-- s 21(1): a document not in accordance with this Part "does not take effect as an advance care directive ... unless VCAT
-- makes an order referred to in section 22(2)(b)(ii)" -- the text's own no (JUST FALSE in substance). s 21(2): it may still
-- be taken into account as a statement of preferences and values. s 22(2)(b): VCAT may declare it invalid, or valid "if a
-- person's intention to give ... is sufficiently clear" (VCAT's judgment, the order asked as a fact). Fork F1: s 13(a) read
-- as a "requirement of this Part" VCAT can excuse.
GIVEN `my age when I gave it` IS A NUMBER
      `I had capacity for and understood each statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in writing in English with my full name, date of birth and address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signer` IS A `Who signed the document`
      `the number of adult witnesses` IS A NUMBER
      `each witness signed and dated it in my presence and each other's` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a witness is a registered medical practitioner who wrote that qualification on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a witness is my appointed medical treatment decision maker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a witness has the prescribed training and experience` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each witness certified as s 17(2) and (3) require` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was induced by dishonesty or undue influence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the VCAT order` IS A `VCAT order on validity`
GIVETH A `Whether my advance care directive is valid`
`ss 13, 16, 17, 21, 22 -- whether my advance care directive is valid` `my age when I gave it` `I had capacity for and understood each statement` `in writing in English with my full name, date of birth and address` `the signer` `the number of adult witnesses` `each witness signed and dated it in my presence and each other's` `a witness is a registered medical practitioner who wrote that qualification on it` `a witness is my appointed medical treatment decision maker` `a witness has the prescribed training and experience` `each witness certified as s 17(2) and (3) require` `I was induced by dishonesty or undue influence` `the VCAT order` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I was induced by dishonesty or undue influence`
           THEN `void: I was induced to give it by dishonesty or undue influence (s 14(2))`
           IF `the VCAT order` EQUALS `VCAT declared it invalid`
           THEN `invalid: VCAT declared it invalid (s 22(2)(b)(i))`
           IF `the failure` EQUALS NOTHING
           THEN `valid: it came into force when it was signed (ss 13, 16, 17, 19(1))`
           IF `the VCAT order` EQUALS `VCAT declared it valid despite a failure to comply`
           THEN `valid: VCAT declared it valid despite a failure to comply (s 22(2)(b)(ii))`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `the failure`
               WHEN JUST f THEN f
               WHEN NOTHING THEN `valid: it came into force when it was signed (ss 13, 16, 17, 19(1))`
    WHERE
        `properly signed` MEANS
               `the signer` EQUALS `I signed it myself`
            OR `the signer` EQUALS `an adult who is not a witness signed it at my direction`
        `properly witnessed` MEANS
                `the number of adult witnesses` AT LEAST 2
            AND `each witness signed and dated it in my presence and each other's`
            AND `a witness is a registered medical practitioner who wrote that qualification on it`
            AND (NOT `a witness is my appointed medical treatment decision maker`)
            AND (`s 3 -- an adult` `my age when I gave it` OR `a witness has the prescribed training and experience`)
        `the failure` MEANS
            BRANCH IF NOT `I had capacity for and understood each statement`
                   THEN JUST `no effect as a directive: I lacked capacity for, or did not understand, a statement in it (s 13(a), s 21(1))`
                   IF NOT `in writing in English with my full name, date of birth and address`
                   THEN JUST `no effect as a directive: it is not in writing in English with my full name, date of birth and address (s 16(1)(a), (b), s 21(1))`
                   IF NOT `properly signed`
                   THEN JUST `no effect as a directive: it was not properly signed (s 16(1)(c), (2), s 21(1))`
                   IF NOT `properly witnessed`
                   THEN JUST `no effect as a directive: the witnessing did not meet s 17(1) (s 21(1))`
                   IF NOT `each witness certified as s 17(2) and (3) require`
                   THEN JUST `no effect as a directive: the witnesses did not certify as s 17(2) and (3) require (s 21(1))`
                   OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Part 2 -- when an advance care directive is in force (ss 19, 20, 22(2)(a))`

DECLARE `How my directive was revoked` IS ONE OF
    `not revoked`
    `revoked by a later advance care directive I gave (s 20(3))`
    `revoked by a revocation made with the formalities of Part 2 (s 20(1))`
    `revoked in whole by VCAT (s 22(2)(a)(i))`

DECLARE `Whether my advance care directive is in force` IS ONE OF
    `not yet in force: it has not been signed in accordance with Part 2 by that day (s 19(1))`
    `in force (s 19)`
    `suspended by VCAT for that day (s 22(2)(a)(iii))`
    `no longer in force: its expiry date has been reached (s 19(2)(a))`
    `no longer in force: it has been revoked (s 19(2)(b))`

-- s 19(1): "An advance care directive comes into force at the time it is signed in accordance with this Part." (2): "remains
-- in force until -- (a) any expiry date that is specified in it; or (b) it is revoked in accordance with this Act."
-- s 20(3): "An advance care directive given by a person is revoked by any later advance care directive given by that
-- person." Fork F2: "until any expiry date" read as ending at the start of the expiry date (not in force on it). The
-- directive is taken as validly made (the validity question answers that).
GIVEN `the day it was signed` IS A DATE
      `it specifies an expiry date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expiry date` IS A DATE
      `the revocation` IS A `How my directive was revoked`
      `the day it was revoked` IS A DATE
      `VCAT has suspended it for a period that includes the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Whether my advance care directive is in force`
`ss 19, 20, 22 -- whether my advance care directive is in force` `the day it was signed` `it specifies an expiry date` `the expiry date` `the revocation` `the day it was revoked` `VCAT has suspended it for a period that includes the day` `the day asked about` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the days from` `the day it was signed` `to` `the day asked about` LESS THAN 0
           THEN `not yet in force: it has not been signed in accordance with Part 2 by that day (s 19(1))`
           IF (NOT (`the revocation` EQUALS `not revoked`)) AND `the days from` `the day it was revoked` `to` `the day asked about` AT LEAST 0
           THEN `no longer in force: it has been revoked (s 19(2)(b))`
           IF `it specifies an expiry date` AND `the days from` `the expiry date` `to` `the day asked about` AT LEAST 0
           THEN `no longer in force: its expiry date has been reached (s 19(2)(a))`
           IF `VCAT has suspended it for a period that includes the day`
           THEN `suspended by VCAT for that day (s 22(2)(a)(iii))`
           OTHERWISE `in force (s 19)`

§§ `Part 2 -- what a statement in my directive is (ss 6, 8A, 12, 18)`

DECLARE `What the statement is about` IS ONE OF
    `medical treatment or a medical research procedure`
    `consent to a special medical procedure`
    `palliative care`
    `voluntary assisted dying`

DECLARE `What my statement is` IS ONE OF
    `void and severed from the directive: an unlawful or prohibited statement (s 18(2))`
    `not authorised by this Act: voluntary assisted dying (s 8A)`
    `an instructional directive: it takes effect as if I had consented to or refused the treatment myself (s 6(1))`
    `a values directive: my preferences and values, which my decision maker and practitioners must consider (ss 6(2), 12(3))`

-- s 12(3): "each of the following is a values directive -- (a) any statement that is not expressly identified on the face
-- of the document as an instructional directive; (b) any instructional directive that is of unclear or uncertain
-- application in relation to particular circumstances ...; (c) any statement -- (i) purporting to consent to a special
-- medical procedure; or (ii) concerning palliative care; or (iii) made in a document of another State or a Territory
-- recognised as an advance care directive under section 95."
-- s 18(1): must not include "(a) a statement that is unlawful or would require an unlawful act to be performed; (b) a
-- statement that would, if given effect, cause a health practitioner to contravene a professional standard or code of
-- conduct ...; (c) a statement -- (i) of a prescribed kind; or (ii) containing a prescribed instruction". (2): "that
-- statement is void and is severed from the directive". No regulations are deposited: "prescribed" is asked as a fact.
-- s 8A: "Nothing in this Act authorises the making of ... (a) a statement in an advance care directive" about voluntary
-- assisted dying.
GIVEN `the subject` IS A `What the statement is about`
      `expressly identified on the face of the document as an instructional directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `clear in its application to the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `made in an interstate document recognised under s 95` IS A BOOLEAN
      `unlawful or would require an unlawful act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would make a practitioner breach a professional standard or code of conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `of a prescribed kind or containing a prescribed instruction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What my statement is`
`ss 6, 8A, 12, 18 -- what my statement is` `the subject` `expressly identified on the face of the document as an instructional directive` `clear in its application to the circumstances` `made in an interstate document recognised under s 95` `unlawful or would require an unlawful act` `would make a practitioner breach a professional standard or code of conduct` `of a prescribed kind or containing a prescribed instruction` MEANS
    BRANCH IF    `unlawful or would require an unlawful act`
              OR `would make a practitioner breach a professional standard or code of conduct`
              OR `of a prescribed kind or containing a prescribed instruction`
           THEN `void and severed from the directive: an unlawful or prohibited statement (s 18(2))`
           IF `the subject` EQUALS `voluntary assisted dying`
           THEN `not authorised by this Act: voluntary assisted dying (s 8A)`
           IF     `expressly identified on the face of the document as an instructional directive`
              AND `clear in its application to the circumstances`
              AND `the subject` EQUALS `medical treatment or a medical research procedure`
              AND (NOT `made in an interstate document recognised under s 95`)
           THEN `an instructional directive: it takes effect as if I had consented to or refused the treatment myself (s 6(1))`
           OTHERWISE `a values directive: my preferences and values, which my decision maker and practitioners must consider (ss 6(2), 12(3))`

§§ `Part 3 -- appointing a medical treatment decision maker or a support person (ss 26-37, 42-45)`

DECLARE `Kind of appointment` IS ONE OF
    `an appointed medical treatment decision maker`
    `a support person`

DECLARE `VCAT order on an appointment` IS ONE OF
    `no VCAT order about the appointment`
    `VCAT declared the attempt to appoint effective (ss 43(2)(b)(ii), 45)`
    `VCAT declared the appointment invalid (s 43(2)(b)(i))`

DECLARE `Whether my appointment is valid` IS ONE OF
    `void: I was induced to make it by dishonesty or undue influence (s 42(2))`
    `invalid: VCAT declared it invalid (s 43(2)(b)(i))`
    `effective: VCAT declared it effective despite non-compliance (s 45)`
    `valid and in effect (ss 28, 33, 38(1))`
    `made, but not yet in effect: each appointee must first accept it in writing (ss 28(1)(g), 29, 33(f), 34)`
    `not covered: the Act gives this power only to an adult with capacity appointing an adult (s 26(1))`
    `not covered: the Act gives this power only to a person with capacity (s 31(1))`
    `not validly made: it is not in writing in English with my details and any prescribed details (s 28(1)(a)-(c), s 33(a)-(c))`
    `not validly made: it was not properly signed (ss 28(1)(d), 33(d), 37)`
    `not validly made: the witnessing did not meet s 36(1)`
    `not validly made: the witnesses did not certify as s 36(2) requires`

-- s 26(1): "An adult who has decision-making capacity may appoint another adult as the person's appointed medical
-- treatment decision maker." s 31(1): "Any person (including a child) who has decision-making capacity may appoint another
-- person (including a child) as the person's support person." A grant limited in its own words: outside it, NOTHING-kind
-- ("not covered").
-- s 28(1) and s 33: in writing in English; the maker's full name, date of birth and address; any prescribed details of
-- each appointee (regulations not deposited: one input); signed by the maker, subject to s 37; witnessed and certified under
-- s 36; "must be accepted by each appointee in accordance with section 29 [s 34] before it comes into effect".
-- s 37: another may sign at the maker's direction if "(a) is an adult; and (b) is not a witness ...; and (c) is not an
-- appointee".
-- s 36(1): "(a) 2 adult witnesses ...; (b) each witness must sign and date the document in the presence of -- (i) the person
-- making ... the appointment; and (ii) each other; (c) at least one of the witnesses must be an authorised witness [a
-- registered medical practitioner, or an authorised affidavit taker under the Oaths and Affirmations Act 2018] and must
-- write the qualification ... on the document." (2): the certifications, including "(d) the witness is not an appointee
-- under the appointment".
-- s 42(2) (decision makers only): an appointment induced by dishonesty or undue influence "is void and of no effect".
-- Fork F3: a bare "must" in s 28 or s 33 not met is answered "not validly made" (s 45 speaks of "the attempt to make a
-- valid appointment despite any non-compliance"). Fork F4: s 42(2) does not reach a support person; inducement then
-- leaves only VCAT's power under s 44(c).
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of appointment`
      `my age when I made it` IS A NUMBER
      `I had capacity when I made it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointee's age` IS A NUMBER
      `in writing in English with my details and any prescribed details of each appointee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signer` IS A `Who signed the document`
      `the number of adult witnesses` IS A NUMBER
      `each witness signed and dated it in my presence and each other's` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a witness is an authorised witness who wrote that qualification on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a witness is an appointee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each witness certified as s 36(2) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each appointee accepted it in writing on the same document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was induced by dishonesty or undue influence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the VCAT order` IS A `VCAT order on an appointment`
GIVETH A `Whether my appointment is valid`
`ss 26-45 -- whether my appointment is valid` `the kind` `my age when I made it` `I had capacity when I made it` `the appointee's age` `in writing in English with my details and any prescribed details of each appointee` `the signer` `the number of adult witnesses` `each witness signed and dated it in my presence and each other's` `a witness is an authorised witness who wrote that qualification on it` `a witness is an appointee` `each witness certified as s 36(2) requires` `each appointee accepted it in writing on the same document` `I was induced by dishonesty or undue influence` `the VCAT order` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I was induced by dishonesty or undue influence` AND `the kind` EQUALS `an appointed medical treatment decision maker`
           THEN `void: I was induced to make it by dishonesty or undue influence (s 42(2))`
           IF `the VCAT order` EQUALS `VCAT declared the appointment invalid (s 43(2)(b)(i))`
           THEN `invalid: VCAT declared it invalid (s 43(2)(b)(i))`
           IF `the VCAT order` EQUALS `VCAT declared the attempt to appoint effective (ss 43(2)(b)(ii), 45)`
           THEN `effective: VCAT declared it effective despite non-compliance (s 45)`
           IF `the kind` EQUALS `an appointed medical treatment decision maker`
              AND (NOT (    `s 3 -- an adult` `my age when I made it`
                        AND `I had capacity when I made it`
                        AND `s 3 -- an adult` `the appointee's age`))
           THEN `not covered: the Act gives this power only to an adult with capacity appointing an adult (s 26(1))`
           IF `the kind` EQUALS `a support person` AND (NOT `I had capacity when I made it`)
           THEN `not covered: the Act gives this power only to a person with capacity (s 31(1))`
           IF NOT `in writing in English with my details and any prescribed details of each appointee`
           THEN `not validly made: it is not in writing in English with my details and any prescribed details (s 28(1)(a)-(c), s 33(a)-(c))`
           IF NOT (   `the signer` EQUALS `I signed it myself`
                   OR `the signer` EQUALS `an adult who is not a witness signed it at my direction`)
           THEN `not validly made: it was not properly signed (ss 28(1)(d), 33(d), 37)`
           IF NOT (    `the number of adult witnesses` AT LEAST 2
                   AND `each witness signed and dated it in my presence and each other's`
                   AND `a witness is an authorised witness who wrote that qualification on it`)
           THEN `not validly made: the witnessing did not meet s 36(1)`
           IF `a witness is an appointee` OR (NOT `each witness certified as s 36(2) requires`)
           THEN `not validly made: the witnesses did not certify as s 36(2) requires`
           IF NOT `each appointee accepted it in writing on the same document`
           THEN `made, but not yet in effect: each appointee must first accept it in writing (ss 28(1)(g), 29, 33(f), 34)`
           OTHERWISE `valid and in effect (ss 28, 33, 38(1))`

§§ `Part 3 -- whether my appointment is still in force (ss 30, 35, 38, 39, 43(2)(a))`

DECLARE `My revocation of the appointment` IS ONE OF
    `I have not revoked it`
    `I revoked it with capacity and with the formalities of s 28(1) or s 33`
    `I tried to revoke it without capacity for that decision`
    `I tried to revoke it without the formalities`

DECLARE `The appointee's resignation` IS ONE OF
    `the appointee has not resigned`
    `the appointee resigned in writing, signed, dated and witnessed by one adult (s 39(4))`
    `the appointee said they resign, without meeting s 39(4)`

DECLARE `Whether my appointment is in force` IS ONE OF
    `in force (s 38)`
    `revoked by me (ss 30, 35(1), 38(2)(a))`
    `revoked by my later appointment of a support person (s 35(2))`
    `ended: the appointee resigned (ss 38(2)(b), 39)`
    `revoked by VCAT (s 43(2)(a)(i))`
    `in force: my attempted revocation was without capacity, so s 30 or s 35(1) does not let me revoke it`
    `in force: my attempted revocation lacked the formalities, unless VCAT declares it effective (s 43(2)(b)(ii))`

-- s 30 (decision makers), s 35(1) (support persons): the maker "may revoke that appointment -- (a) if the person has
-- decision-making capacity in relation to the revocation decision; and (b) by complying with the requirements ... set out
-- in section 28(1) [section 33], other than paragraph (g) [(f)]". An "if" that fails: no revocation. s 35(2): "An
-- appointment of a support person is revoked by any later appointment of a support person." s 38(2): in force until
-- "(a) it is revoked in accordance with this Act; or (b) the appointee resigns". s 39(4): a resignation "must be in
-- writing ...; must be signed and dated ...; must be witnessed by one adult witness". Fork F5: a resignation that does not
-- meet s 39(4) leaves the appointment in force. s 39(3): failing to inform the maker does not affect a resignation; s 40(2):
-- failing to inform the appointee does not affect a revocation; neither is an input.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of appointment`
      `my revocation` IS A `My revocation of the appointment`
      `I later appointed another support person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resignation` IS A `The appointee's resignation`
      `VCAT has revoked it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether my appointment is in force`
`ss 30, 35, 38, 39 -- whether my appointment is in force` `the kind` `my revocation` `I later appointed another support person` `the resignation` `VCAT has revoked it` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `VCAT has revoked it`
           THEN `revoked by VCAT (s 43(2)(a)(i))`
           IF `my revocation` EQUALS `I revoked it with capacity and with the formalities of s 28(1) or s 33`
           THEN `revoked by me (ss 30, 35(1), 38(2)(a))`
           IF `the kind` EQUALS `a support person` AND `I later appointed another support person`
           THEN `revoked by my later appointment of a support person (s 35(2))`
           IF `the resignation` EQUALS `the appointee resigned in writing, signed, dated and witnessed by one adult (s 39(4))`
           THEN `ended: the appointee resigned (ss 38(2)(b), 39)`
           IF `my revocation` EQUALS `I tried to revoke it without capacity for that decision`
           THEN `in force: my attempted revocation was without capacity, so s 30 or s 35(1) does not let me revoke it`
           IF `my revocation` EQUALS `I tried to revoke it without the formalities`
           THEN `in force: my attempted revocation lacked the formalities, unless VCAT declares it effective (s 43(2)(b)(ii))`
           OTHERWISE `in force (s 38)`

§§ `Part 4 Division 1 -- who is my medical treatment decision maker (s 55, with ss 28(2), 102(2), 103)`

DECLARE `Who my medical treatment decision maker is` IS ONE OF
    `s 55 does not apply while I am a mental health patient (s 55(5)); see the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022`
    `my appointed medical treatment decision maker: the first listed appointee who is reasonably available and willing and able (ss 28(2), 55(1))`
    `my guardian appointed by VCAT with power to make medical treatment decisions (s 55(2))`
    `my spouse or domestic partner (s 55(3)(a))`
    `my primary carer (s 55(3)(b))`
    `my oldest adult child who qualifies (s 55(3)(c)(i))`
    `my oldest parent who qualifies (s 55(3)(c)(ii))`
    `my oldest adult sibling who qualifies (s 55(3)(c)(iii))`
    `my parent, guardian or other person with parental responsibility for me (s 55(4))`
    `nobody: I have no medical treatment decision maker for this decision (s 55)`

-- s 55(1): "If an adult has an appointed medical treatment decision maker, the appointee is the person's medical treatment
-- decision maker if the appointee is reasonably available and willing and able to make the medical treatment decision."
-- s 28(2): the first person listed who is so available. ss 102(2), 103: an agent under a Medical Treatment Act 1988
-- enduring power, and an attorney or enduring guardian with medical treatment power, are taken to be appointed medical
-- treatment decision makers (the seat's input says so).
-- (2): a VCAT-appointed guardian under the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 with power to make medical treatment
-- decisions, if reasonably available and willing and able.
-- (3): "the first of the following persons who is in a close and continuing relationship with the person and who, in the
-- circumstances, is reasonably available and willing and able ... -- (a) the spouse or domestic partner ...; (b) the
-- primary carer ...; (c) the first of the following and, if more than one person fits the description ..., the oldest of
-- those persons -- (i) an adult child ...; (ii) a parent ...; (iii) an adult sibling". Each category's input means: someone
-- in it who is in a close and continuing relationship and reasonably available and willing and able (judgments, asked).
-- (4): for a child, the parent or guardian or other person with parental responsibility who is reasonably available and
-- willing and able. (5): (1)-(4) "do not apply at any time that the person is a mental health patient".
-- The definition (s 3: "the person identified in accordance with section 55") is a "means" definition: where nobody
-- qualifies, the person has no medical treatment decision maker (JUST FALSE in substance).
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `I am a mental health patient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appointee of mine is available and willing and able` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a VCAT-appointed guardian with medical treatment power is available and willing and able` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse or domestic partner qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my primary carer qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult child of mine qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a parent of mine qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult sibling of mine qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who my medical treatment decision maker is`
`s 55 -- who my medical treatment decision maker is` `my age` `I am a mental health patient` `an appointee of mine is available and willing and able` `a VCAT-appointed guardian with medical treatment power is available and willing and able` `my spouse or domestic partner qualifies` `my primary carer qualifies` `an adult child of mine qualifies` `a parent of mine qualifies` `an adult sibling of mine qualifies` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I am a mental health patient`
           THEN `s 55 does not apply while I am a mental health patient (s 55(5)); see the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022`
           IF `s 3 -- an adult` `my age` AND `an appointee of mine is available and willing and able`
           THEN `my appointed medical treatment decision maker: the first listed appointee who is reasonably available and willing and able (ss 28(2), 55(1))`
           IF `a VCAT-appointed guardian with medical treatment power is available and willing and able`
           THEN `my guardian appointed by VCAT with power to make medical treatment decisions (s 55(2))`
           IF NOT `s 3 -- an adult` `my age`
           THEN IF `a parent of mine qualifies`
                THEN `my parent, guardian or other person with parental responsibility for me (s 55(4))`
                ELSE `nobody: I have no medical treatment decision maker for this decision (s 55)`
           IF `my spouse or domestic partner qualifies`
           THEN `my spouse or domestic partner (s 55(3)(a))`
           IF `my primary carer qualifies`
           THEN `my primary carer (s 55(3)(b))`
           IF `an adult child of mine qualifies`
           THEN `my oldest adult child who qualifies (s 55(3)(c)(i))`
           IF `a parent of mine qualifies`
           THEN `my oldest parent who qualifies (s 55(3)(c)(ii))`
           IF `an adult sibling of mine qualifies`
           THEN `my oldest adult sibling who qualifies (s 55(3)(c)(iii))`
           OTHERWISE `nobody: I have no medical treatment decision maker for this decision (s 55)`

-- The same answer reduced to whether anybody is the decision maker (used by Part 4 Division 2 and Part 5).
GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Who my medical treatment decision maker is`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a medical treatment decision maker` `the answer` IF
        (NOT (`the answer` EQUALS `nobody: I have no medical treatment decision maker for this decision (s 55)`))
    AND (NOT (`the answer` EQUALS `s 55 does not apply while I am a mental health patient (s 55(5)); see the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022`))

§§ `Part 4 -- whether I may be given medical treatment while I lack capacity (ss 48, 51, 54, 57-63)`

DECLARE `Kind of treatment` IS ONE OF
    `ordinary medical treatment`
    `palliative care`
    `a special medical procedure`
    `treatment for mental illness while I am a mental health patient`
    `neurosurgery for mental illness`

DECLARE `My instructional directive on this treatment` IS ONE OF
    `no relevant instructional directive`
    `my instructional directive consents to it`
    `my instructional directive refuses it`

DECLARE `My decision maker's decision` IS ONE OF
    `my decision maker has not decided yet`
    `my decision maker consents`
    `my decision maker refuses`

DECLARE `Whether I may be given the treatment` IS ONE OF
    `not this Part: I have decision-making capacity for this decision, so the decision is mine`
    `not this Part: Part 4 does not apply to treatment for mental illness while I am a mental health patient, or to neurosurgery for mental illness (s 48(1))`
    `not this Division: a special medical procedure is dealt with under Part 6 of the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (s 57(2))`
    `palliative care: it may be given despite my decision maker's decision, with regard to my preferences and values and after consulting my decision maker (s 54)`
    `yes, before I recover: my directive or my decision maker consents and delay would significantly worsen my condition (s 59)`
    `no: not before I recover capacity, which is likely within a reasonable time (s 59)`
    `no: my instructional directive refuses it, and it must be withheld or withdrawn (s 60(1)(a)(i))`
    `the practitioner may refuse to follow my instructional directive's refusal (s 51)`
    `yes: my instructional directive consents and the practitioner thinks it clinically appropriate (s 60(1)(a)(ii))`
    `my instructional directive consents, but the practitioner need not give it: not clinically appropriate (ss 8, 60(1)(a)(ii))`
    `yes: my medical treatment decision maker consents (ss 58, 61)`
    `no: my medical treatment decision maker refuses (ss 58, 61)`
    `only if my medical treatment decision maker consents (ss 58, 60(1)(b), 61)`
    `yes, without consent: routine treatment, with no directive and no decision maker found (s 63(1)(a))`
    `yes: significant treatment the Public Advocate has consented to (s 63(1)(b), (2))`
    `only if the Public Advocate consents: significant treatment, with no directive and no decision maker found (s 63(1)(b))`
    `not covered: I am a mental health patient, so s 63 does not apply (s 63(3)); see the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022`
    `not covered: I have a directive with no relevant instructional directive and no decision maker was found; s 63 speaks only where neither is located`

-- s 48(1): Part 4 "does not apply in relation to -- (a) medical treatment that is treatment for mental illness at any time
-- that the person being treated is a mental health patient; (b) neurosurgery for mental illness."
-- s 54: palliative care may be given to a person without capacity "despite any decision of the person's medical treatment
-- decision maker", having regard to preferences and values and consulting the decision maker. s 57: Division 2 does not
-- apply to palliative care or a special medical procedure.
-- s 58(1): for treatment to which Division 2 applies, "a medical treatment decision must be obtained or ascertained in
-- accordance with this Division".
-- s 59: where the person "is likely to recover decision-making capacity for that decision within a reasonable time, the
-- health practitioner may only administer the medical treatment before the person recovers ... if -- (a) the medical
-- treatment -- (i) is in accordance with any relevant instructional directive; or (ii) has been consented to by the
-- person's medical treatment decision maker; and (b) the health practitioner reasonably believes that a further delay ...
-- would result in a significant deterioration of the person's condition." "May only ... if": JUST FALSE when it fails.
-- s 60(1)(a): "subject to section 51, give effect to any relevant instructional directive by -- (i) ... refusing ...,
-- withholding or withdrawing that medical treatment; and (ii) ... consenting ..., administering that medical treatment if
-- the health practitioner is of the opinion that it is clinically appropriate to do so"; (b) where there is no relevant
-- instructional directive, refer the decision to the medical treatment decision maker under s 61.
-- s 51: the practitioner "may refuse ... to comply with an instructional directive if the health practitioner believes on
-- reasonable grounds that -- (a) circumstances have changed ... so that the practical effect of the instructional directive
-- would no longer be consistent with the person's preferences and values; and (b) the delay that would be caused by an
-- application to VCAT under section 22 would result in a significant deterioration of the person's condition."
-- s 63(1): "despite having complied with section 50, has not been able to locate an advance care directive or a medical
-- treatment decision maker ... -- (a) if the medical treatment is routine treatment, the health practitioner may administer
-- that routine treatment without consent; or (b) if ... significant treatment, the health practitioner may only administer
-- that significant treatment if the Public Advocate consents". (3): not "at any time that the person is a mental health
-- patient". Fork F6: s 63 read as applying only where neither a directive nor a decision maker was located; a directive
-- with values only and no decision maker is then a gap (NOTHING-kind). Fork F7: s 59 is applied before s 60 and s 63, so a
-- person likely to recover soon gets no routine treatment under s 63(1)(a) unless s 59 is met.
-- s 50 (reasonable efforts to find a directive and a decision maker) is taken as complied with. s 53 (emergencies) is a
-- separate question.
GIVEN `I have capacity for this decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a mental health patient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of treatment`
      `significant bodily intrusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `significant risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `significant side effects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `significant distress` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am likely to recover capacity for this decision within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `further delay would significantly worsen my condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a directive of mine was located` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my instructional directive` IS A `My instructional directive on this treatment`
      `the practitioner believes circumstances have changed so my directive no longer fits my preferences and values` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner believes the delay of a VCAT application would significantly worsen my condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner thinks the treatment clinically appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a decision maker of mine was located` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision` IS A `My decision maker's decision`
      `the Public Advocate consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether I may be given the treatment`
`Part 4 -- whether I may be given the treatment` `I have capacity for this decision` `I am a mental health patient` `the kind` `significant bodily intrusion` `significant risk` `significant side effects` `significant distress` `I am likely to recover capacity for this decision within a reasonable time` `further delay would significantly worsen my condition` `a directive of mine was located` `my instructional directive` `the practitioner believes circumstances have changed so my directive no longer fits my preferences and values` `the practitioner believes the delay of a VCAT application would significantly worsen my condition` `the practitioner thinks the treatment clinically appropriate` `a decision maker of mine was located` `the decision` `the Public Advocate consents` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I have capacity for this decision`
           THEN `not this Part: I have decision-making capacity for this decision, so the decision is mine`
           IF    `the kind` EQUALS `treatment for mental illness while I am a mental health patient`
              OR `the kind` EQUALS `neurosurgery for mental illness`
           THEN `not this Part: Part 4 does not apply to treatment for mental illness while I am a mental health patient, or to neurosurgery for mental illness (s 48(1))`
           IF `the kind` EQUALS `a special medical procedure`
           THEN `not this Division: a special medical procedure is dealt with under Part 6 of the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (s 57(2))`
           IF `the kind` EQUALS `palliative care`
           THEN `palliative care: it may be given despite my decision maker's decision, with regard to my preferences and values and after consulting my decision maker (s 54)`
           IF `I am likely to recover capacity for this decision within a reasonable time`
           THEN IF     (   `the ID consents`
                        OR (`a decision maker of mine was located` AND `the decision` EQUALS `my decision maker consents`))
                   AND `further delay would significantly worsen my condition`
                THEN `yes, before I recover: my directive or my decision maker consents and delay would significantly worsen my condition (s 59)`
                ELSE `no: not before I recover capacity, which is likely within a reasonable time (s 59)`
           IF `the ID refuses`
           THEN IF     `the practitioner believes circumstances have changed so my directive no longer fits my preferences and values`
                   AND `the practitioner believes the delay of a VCAT application would significantly worsen my condition`
                THEN `the practitioner may refuse to follow my instructional directive's refusal (s 51)`
                ELSE `no: my instructional directive refuses it, and it must be withheld or withdrawn (s 60(1)(a)(i))`
           IF `the ID consents`
           THEN IF `the practitioner thinks the treatment clinically appropriate`
                THEN `yes: my instructional directive consents and the practitioner thinks it clinically appropriate (s 60(1)(a)(ii))`
                ELSE `my instructional directive consents, but the practitioner need not give it: not clinically appropriate (ss 8, 60(1)(a)(ii))`
           IF `a decision maker of mine was located`
           THEN CONSIDER `the decision`
                WHEN `my decision maker consents` THEN `yes: my medical treatment decision maker consents (ss 58, 61)`
                WHEN `my decision maker refuses` THEN `no: my medical treatment decision maker refuses (ss 58, 61)`
                WHEN `my decision maker has not decided yet` THEN `only if my medical treatment decision maker consents (ss 58, 60(1)(b), 61)`
           IF `I am a mental health patient`
           THEN `not covered: I am a mental health patient, so s 63 does not apply (s 63(3)); see the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022`
           IF `a directive of mine was located`
           THEN `not covered: I have a directive with no relevant instructional directive and no decision maker was found; s 63 speaks only where neither is located`
           IF NOT `s 3 -- significant treatment` `significant bodily intrusion` `significant risk` `significant side effects` `significant distress`
           THEN `yes, without consent: routine treatment, with no directive and no decision maker found (s 63(1)(a))`
           IF `the Public Advocate consents`
           THEN `yes: significant treatment the Public Advocate has consented to (s 63(1)(b), (2))`
           OTHERWISE `only if the Public Advocate consents: significant treatment, with no directive and no decision maker found (s 63(1)(b))`
    WHERE
        `the ID consents` MEANS `my instructional directive` EQUALS `my instructional directive consents to it`
        `the ID refuses` MEANS `my instructional directive` EQUALS `my instructional directive refuses it`

§§ `Part 4 -- emergencies (s 53)`

DECLARE `Whether I may be treated in an emergency without consent` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the practitioner believes on reasonable grounds it is urgently necessary (s 53(1))`
    `no: the practitioner knows I have refused this treatment (s 53(2))`
    `not covered by s 53: electroconvulsive treatment is excluded from it (s 53(1))`
    `no: s 53 does not apply, as the practitioner does not believe it urgently necessary for any of its purposes (s 53(1))`

-- s 53(1): a practitioner "may administer medical treatment (other than electroconvulsive treatment) or a medical research
-- procedure to a person without consent ... if the practitioner believes on reasonable grounds that [it] is necessary, as a
-- matter of urgency to -- (a) save the person's life; or (b) prevent serious damage to the person's health; or (c) prevent
-- the person from suffering or continuing to suffer significant pain or distress." (2): "is not permitted ... if the
-- practitioner is aware that the person has refused the particular medical treatment or procedure, whether by way of an
-- instructional directive or a legally valid and informed refusal". (3): no duty to search for a directive not readily
-- available. Fork F8: "(other than electroconvulsive treatment)" answered "not covered by s 53" (NOTHING-kind) rather than a
-- flat no.
GIVEN `it is electroconvulsive treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `urgently necessary to save my life` IS A BOOLEAN
      `urgently necessary to prevent serious damage to my health` IS A BOOLEAN
      `urgently necessary to prevent significant pain or distress` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner is aware I refused this treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether I may be treated in an emergency without consent`
`s 53 -- whether I may be treated in an emergency without consent` `it is electroconvulsive treatment` `urgently necessary to save my life` `urgently necessary to prevent serious damage to my health` `urgently necessary to prevent significant pain or distress` `the practitioner is aware I refused this treatment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it is electroconvulsive treatment`
           THEN `not covered by s 53: electroconvulsive treatment is excluded from it (s 53(1))`
           IF NOT (   `urgently necessary to save my life`
                   OR `urgently necessary to prevent serious damage to my health`
                   OR `urgently necessary to prevent significant pain or distress`)
           THEN `no: s 53 does not apply, as the practitioner does not believe it urgently necessary for any of its purposes (s 53(1))`
           IF `the practitioner is aware I refused this treatment`
           THEN `no: the practitioner knows I have refused this treatment (s 53(2))`
           OTHERWISE `yes: the practitioner believes on reasonable grounds it is urgently necessary (s 53(1))`

§§ `Part 4 -- the Public Advocate after my decision maker refuses significant treatment (ss 62, 67)`

-- s 62: "A health practitioner must notify the Public Advocate if -- (a) the medical treatment decision maker of a person
-- refuses significant treatment under section 61; and (b) the health practitioner reasonably believes that the preferences
-- and values of the person are not known or are unable to be known or inferred by that medical treatment decision maker."
-- An "if" condition: JUST FALSE when it fails.
GIVEN `my decision maker refused significant treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner believes my preferences and values are not known to my decision maker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62 -- the practitioner must notify the Public Advocate` `my decision maker refused significant treatment` `the practitioner believes my preferences and values are not known to my decision maker` MEANS
    IF `my decision maker refused significant treatment` AND `the practitioner believes my preferences and values are not known to my decision maker`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 67(2): if the Public Advocate "is of the opinion that the decision ... to refuse the medical treatment is unreasonable
-- in the circumstances, the Public Advocate, as soon as practicable but not more than 14 days after receiving that
-- notification, must apply to VCAT for a review of that decision." (1): if of the opinion it is not unreasonable, it must
-- tell the practitioner that no application will be made. The last day: the day of notification excluded, 14 days on.
-- A regulative rule: the Public Advocate MUST apply WITHIN the 14 days (day 0 the day of notification), LEST BREACH.
DECLARE `Public Advocate party` IS ONE OF `the Public Advocate`
DECLARE `Public Advocate act` IS ONE OF `apply to VCAT for a review of the refusal`

GIVEN `the day the Public Advocate was notified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 67(2) -- the last day for the Public Advocate to apply` `the day the Public Advocate was notified` MEANS
    `the date` 14 `days after` `the day the Public Advocate was notified`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Public Advocate party` `Public Advocate act`
`s 67(2) -- the Public Advocate must apply within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the Public Advocate`
    MUST `apply to VCAT for a review of the refusal`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Public Advocate` BECAUSE "no application to VCAT within 14 days after the s 62 notification, though the Public Advocate thought the refusal unreasonable (s 67(2))"

-- The helper that runs the rule over what happened (as the Wills Act 1997 and County Court Act 1958 encodings do). On the
-- stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: FULFILLED means in time, anything else late.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Public Advocate party` `Public Advocate act`
      `the time it was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Advocate's application is in time under` `the rule` `at` `the time it was made` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was made`), (EVENT `the Public Advocate` `apply to VCAT for a review of the refusal` `the time it was made`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where the Public Advocate's review stands` IS ONE OF
    `no duty to apply: the Public Advocate does not think the refusal unreasonable, and must tell the practitioner so (s 67(1))`
    `applied in time (s 67(2))`
    `still in time: the Public Advocate must apply by the last day (s 67(2))`
    `late: the 14 days after notification have passed (s 67(2))`

GIVEN `the Public Advocate thinks the refusal unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Public Advocate was notified` IS A DATE
      `the Public Advocate has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where the Public Advocate's review stands`
`s 67 -- where the Public Advocate's review stands` `the Public Advocate thinks the refusal unreasonable` `the day the Public Advocate was notified` `the Public Advocate has applied` `the day it applied` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the Public Advocate thinks the refusal unreasonable`
           THEN `no duty to apply: the Public Advocate does not think the refusal unreasonable, and must tell the practitioner so (s 67(1))`
           IF `the Public Advocate's application is in time under` `s 67(2) -- the Public Advocate must apply within 14 days` `at` `the time`
           THEN IF `the Public Advocate has applied` THEN `applied in time (s 67(2))` ELSE `still in time: the Public Advocate must apply by the last day (s 67(2))`
           OTHERWISE `late: the 14 days after notification have passed (s 67(2))`
    WHERE
        `the time` MEANS
            IF `the Public Advocate has applied`
            THEN `the days from` `the day the Public Advocate was notified` `to` `the day it applied`
            ELSE `the days from` `the day the Public Advocate was notified` `to` `today`

§§ `Part 4 -- whether the practitioner is protected from my claim (ss 49, 52)`

DECLARE `The directive the practitioner relied on` IS ONE OF
    `the practitioner did not rely on an instructional directive`
    `relied on my instructional directive, which was in force`
    `relied on my instructional directive, which had been revoked or was invalid, without knowing`
    `relied on my instructional directive, knowing it had been revoked or was invalid`

DECLARE `Whether the practitioner is protected` IS ONE OF
    `protected under s 52(1): not liable in any civil proceeding (or for an offence, unprofessional conduct or a code breach)`
    `protected under s 52(2): acted on my instructional directive; not liable in any civil proceeding because of that treatment or its withholding`
    `this section gives the practitioner no protection on these facts (s 52); the duty of care is unaffected (s 49)`

-- s 52(1): a practitioner "who, in good faith and without negligence, administers or does not administer medical treatment
-- ... under this Part and believes on reasonable grounds that the requirements of this Part have been complied with is not
-- -- ... (c) liable in any civil proceeding". (2): one who, "in good faith, without negligence and in reliance on an
-- instructional directive, administers or does not administer medical treatment that the practitioner believes on
-- reasonable grounds is in accordance with that instructional directive" is likewise not liable. (3): acting in good faith
-- on a revoked or invalid directive "who is not aware of the revocation or invalidity, is to be treated as having acted in
-- good faith in reliance on that directive". s 49: "Nothing in this Part affects any duty of care owed by a health
-- practitioner to a patient." A protection with conditions: when they fail, "this section gives no protection on these
-- facts" (the ruling on defences, (b)), never "no protection at all".
GIVEN `the practitioner acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner acted without negligence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner believed on reasonable grounds that Part 4 was complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reliance` IS A `The directive the practitioner relied on`
      `the practitioner believed on reasonable grounds the treatment accorded with the directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether the practitioner is protected`
`s 52 -- whether the practitioner is protected` `the practitioner acted in good faith` `the practitioner acted without negligence` `the practitioner believed on reasonable grounds that Part 4 was complied with` `the reliance` `the practitioner believed on reasonable grounds the treatment accorded with the directive` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the practitioner acted in good faith` AND `the practitioner acted without negligence`)
           THEN `this section gives the practitioner no protection on these facts (s 52); the duty of care is unaffected (s 49)`
           IF `the practitioner believed on reasonable grounds that Part 4 was complied with`
           THEN `protected under s 52(1): not liable in any civil proceeding (or for an offence, unprofessional conduct or a code breach)`
           IF     (   `the reliance` EQUALS `relied on my instructional directive, which was in force`
                   OR `the reliance` EQUALS `relied on my instructional directive, which had been revoked or was invalid, without knowing`)
              AND `the practitioner believed on reasonable grounds the treatment accorded with the directive`
           THEN `protected under s 52(2): acted on my instructional directive; not liable in any civil proceeding because of that treatment or its withholding`
           OTHERWISE `this section gives the practitioner no protection on these facts (s 52); the duty of care is unaffected (s 49)`

§§ `Part 5 -- medical research procedures while I lack capacity (ss 72, 75, 79, 80, 85)`

DECLARE `Whether a research procedure may be given to me` IS ONE OF
    `not this Part: I have decision-making capacity for it, so it needs my own consent`
    `not covered: Part 5 applies only to adults (s 72(1))`
    `no: the research project has not been approved by its human research ethics committee (ss 75(a), 84)`
    `no: I am likely to recover capacity in time, so it must not be given under Part 5 (s 72(2))`
    `yes: I consented to it in an instructional directive (s 75(b)(i))`
    `no: my instructional directive refuses it, so there is no consent under s 75(b)`
    `yes: my medical treatment decision maker consented (ss 75(b)(ii), 77)`
    `no: my medical treatment decision maker refused (ss 75(b)(ii), 77)`
    `only if my medical treatment decision maker consents (ss 75(b)(ii), 77)`
    `yes, without consent: authorised under Part 5 Division 3 (ss 75(b)(iii), 80)`
    `no: no consent and not authorised under Division 3 (ss 75, 85)`

-- s 72(1): Part 5 "applies to the administration of a medical research procedure to an adult who does not have
-- decision-making capacity in relation to the procedure." (2): if the person "is likely to recover decision-making
-- capacity within a reasonable time ..., a medical research practitioner must not administer the medical research
-- procedure to that person under this Part." s 75: "must not administer ... unless -- (a) the relevant research project has
-- been approved by the relevant human research ethics committee; and (b) subject to section 53 -- (i) the person has
-- consented ... under an instructional directive; or (ii) if there is no relevant instructional directive, the person's
-- medical treatment decision maker has consented ...; or (iii) if the person does not have a medical treatment decision
-- maker, the procedure is authorised under Division 3." s 80(1): Division 3 authorises it where the practitioner believes on
-- reasonable grounds each of (a)-(d), after the reasonable steps of s 79 (one input, the practitioner's judgments).
-- s 53 (emergencies) is the separate question.
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `I have capacity for the procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the project is approved by its human research ethics committee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am likely to recover capacity in time for the project` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my instructional directive` IS A `My instructional directive on this treatment`
      `I have a medical treatment decision maker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision` IS A `My decision maker's decision`
      `the practitioner has met ss 79 and 80` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether a research procedure may be given to me`
`Part 5 -- whether a research procedure may be given to me` `my age` `I have capacity for the procedure` `the project is approved by its human research ethics committee` `I am likely to recover capacity in time for the project` `my instructional directive` `I have a medical treatment decision maker` `the decision` `the practitioner has met ss 79 and 80` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I have capacity for the procedure`
           THEN `not this Part: I have decision-making capacity for it, so it needs my own consent`
           IF NOT `s 3 -- an adult` `my age`
           THEN `not covered: Part 5 applies only to adults (s 72(1))`
           IF NOT `the project is approved by its human research ethics committee`
           THEN `no: the research project has not been approved by its human research ethics committee (ss 75(a), 84)`
           IF `I am likely to recover capacity in time for the project`
           THEN `no: I am likely to recover capacity in time, so it must not be given under Part 5 (s 72(2))`
           IF `my instructional directive` EQUALS `my instructional directive consents to it`
           THEN `yes: I consented to it in an instructional directive (s 75(b)(i))`
           IF `my instructional directive` EQUALS `my instructional directive refuses it`
           THEN `no: my instructional directive refuses it, so there is no consent under s 75(b)`
           IF `I have a medical treatment decision maker`
           THEN CONSIDER `the decision`
                WHEN `my decision maker consents` THEN `yes: my medical treatment decision maker consented (ss 75(b)(ii), 77)`
                WHEN `my decision maker refuses` THEN `no: my medical treatment decision maker refused (ss 75(b)(ii), 77)`
                WHEN `my decision maker has not decided yet` THEN `only if my medical treatment decision maker consents (ss 75(b)(ii), 77)`
           IF `the practitioner has met ss 79 and 80`
           THEN `yes, without consent: authorised under Part 5 Division 3 (ss 75(b)(iii), 80)`
           OTHERWISE `no: no consent and not authorised under Division 3 (ss 75, 85)`

§§ `Part 6 -- rehearings at VCAT (s 88)`

DECLARE `My standing for a rehearing` IS ONE OF
    `I was a party at first instance`
    `I was given notice of the hearing but was not a party`
    `I was neither a party nor given notice`

DECLARE `The order I want reheard` IS ONE OF
    `a final order made at first instance`
    `an interim or temporary order`
    `an order on an application to suspend or revoke the appointment of a decision maker or support person`
    `an order on an application under Part 5 Division 4 (medical research)`
    `an order made by VCAT constituted by the President`
    `an order on an application for a rehearing or for leave`

DECLARE `Whether I may apply for a rehearing` IS ONE OF
    `yes, as a party at first instance (s 88(1)(a))`
    `yes, with VCAT's leave, as a person given notice (s 88(1)(b)(i))`
    `no: this kind of order cannot be reheard (s 88(2))`
    `not covered: s 88(1) gives the right only to a party or a person given notice`

-- s 88(1): "a person may apply to VCAT for a rehearing of an application in relation to which VCAT made an order under this
-- Act -- (a) if the person was a party to the hearing ... at first instance; or (b) if the person was given notice of the
-- hearing ... but was not a party ... -- (i) with the leave of VCAT; or (ii) in the case of the Public Advocate, without
-- seeking the leave of VCAT." (2): "A person is not entitled to apply for a rehearing of any of the following -- (a) an
-- interim order or a temporary order; (b) an application for an order to suspend or revoke the appointment of an appointed
-- medical treatment decision maker or a support person; (c) an application under Division 4 of Part 5; (d) an order made by
-- VCAT constituted by the President ...; (e) an application for a rehearing or leave to apply for a rehearing." The person
-- in the seat is never the Public Advocate. Outside s 88(1) the Act grants nothing and says no more: NOTHING-kind.
GIVEN `my standing` IS A `My standing for a rehearing`
      `the order` IS A `The order I want reheard`
GIVETH A `Whether I may apply for a rehearing`
`s 88(1), (2) -- whether I may apply for a rehearing` `my standing` `the order` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the order` EQUALS `a final order made at first instance`)
           THEN `no: this kind of order cannot be reheard (s 88(2))`
           IF `my standing` EQUALS `I was a party at first instance`
           THEN `yes, as a party at first instance (s 88(1)(a))`
           IF `my standing` EQUALS `I was given notice of the hearing but was not a party`
           THEN `yes, with VCAT's leave, as a person given notice (s 88(1)(b)(i))`
           OTHERWISE `not covered: s 88(1) gives the right only to a party or a person given notice`

-- s 88(3): "An application for a rehearing or for leave to apply for a rehearing must be made within 28 days after the day
-- that the order which is the subject of the rehearing is made." (4): where VCAT gives oral reasons and a party then
-- requests written reasons under s 117 of the VCAT Act 1998, "the day on which the written reasons are given to the party
-- is taken to be the day of the order". The day of the order excluded; the last day is 28 days after it. No extension
-- power appears in this Act. A regulative rule: I DO apply WITHIN 28 days of the day of the order (day 0), LEST BREACH -- the
-- breach being the loss of the right to a rehearing, not a wrong.
DECLARE `Rehearing party` IS ONE OF `the applicant for a rehearing`
DECLARE `Rehearing act` IS ONE OF `apply to VCAT for a rehearing or for leave`

GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
      `written reasons were requested after oral reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the written reasons were given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 88(3), (4) -- the day of the order` `the day the order was made` `written reasons were requested after oral reasons` `the day the written reasons were given` MEANS
    IF `written reasons were requested after oral reasons`
    THEN `the day the written reasons were given`
    ELSE `the day the order was made`

GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 88(3) -- the last day to apply for a rehearing` `the day of the order` MEANS `the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the order`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Rehearing party` `Rehearing act`
`s 88(3) -- apply for a rehearing within 28 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant for a rehearing`
    DO `apply to VCAT for a rehearing or for leave`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant for a rehearing` BECAUSE "no application for a rehearing or for leave within 28 days after the day of the order (s 88(3))"

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Rehearing party` `Rehearing act`
      `the time it was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rehearing application is in time under` `the rule` `at` `the time it was made` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was made`), (EVENT `the applicant for a rehearing` `apply to VCAT for a rehearing or for leave` `the time it was made`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where my rehearing application stands` IS ONE OF
    `made in time (s 88(3))`
    `still open: I can apply in time (s 88(3))`
    `out of time: the 28 days have passed (s 88(3))`

GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where my rehearing application stands`
`s 88(3) -- where my rehearing application stands` `the day of the order` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today` MEANS
    IF `the rehearing application is in time under` `s 88(3) -- apply for a rehearing within 28 days` `at` `the time`
    THEN IF `I have applied` THEN `made in time (s 88(3))` ELSE `still open: I can apply in time (s 88(3))`
    ELSE `out of time: the 28 days have passed (s 88(3))`
    WHERE
        `the time` MEANS
            IF `I have applied`
            THEN `the days from` `the day of the order` `to` `the day I applied`
            ELSE `the days from` `the day of the order` `to` `today`

§§ `Part 7 -- health information (s 94) and interstate instruments (ss 95-97)`

-- s 94(1): "A person's medical treatment decision maker or support person is authorised to access or collect ... health
-- information about the person -- (a) that is relevant to a medical treatment decision to be made by the person, medical
-- treatment decision maker or support person; and (b) that may lawfully be collected by the person." (2): a health
-- practitioner "is authorised to disclose" it to them. An authorisation limited in its own words: outside it, NOTHING.
GIVEN `the requester is my decision maker or support person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is relevant to a medical treatment decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I could lawfully collect it myself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94 -- my decision maker or support person may get my health information` `the requester is my decision maker or support person` `the information is relevant to a medical treatment decision` `I could lawfully collect it myself` MEANS
    IF `the requester is my decision maker or support person` AND `the information is relevant to a medical treatment decision` AND `I could lawfully collect it myself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: an authorisation limited in its own words; s 94 is silent outside it (other law may apply)

DECLARE `Interstate instrument` IS ONE OF
    `an advance care directive made in another State or Territory`
    `an appointment of a decision maker or support person made in another State or Territory`

DECLARE `How far my instrument could have been made in Victoria` IS ONE OF
    `everything in it could validly have been given under this Act`
    `only part of it could validly have been given under this Act`
    `none of it could validly have been given under this Act`

DECLARE `Whether my interstate instrument is recognised` IS ONE OF
    `recognised: taken to be an advance care directive under this Act, but its statements are values directives (ss 95(1), 12(3)(c)(iii))`
    `recognised in part, to the extent it could have been given under this Act; its statements are values directives (ss 95(1), 12(3)(c)(iii), 97)`
    `not recognised as a directive, but it may be considered as my preferences and values (s 95(2))`
    `recognised: taken to be an appointment under Part 3 (s 96(1))`
    `recognised in part, to the extent the powers could have been given under Part 3 (ss 96(1), 97)`
    `not covered: s 96 recognises it only if it complies with the law where it was made and to the extent Part 3 allows`

-- s 95(1): an advance care directive given in another State or a Territory that "complies with the requirements of that
-- other State or the Territory then, to the extent the powers it gives could validly have been given by an advance care
-- directive made under this Act, ... is taken to be an advance care directive given under, and in compliance with, this
-- Act." (2): if not recognised, wholly or partly, it "may nevertheless be taken into consideration ... as an expression of a
-- person's preferences and values". (4): includes "an instrument in the nature of an advance care directive". s 96(1): the
-- same for appointments, "to the extent that the powers the instrument of appointment gives could validly have been given
-- by an appointment under Part 3". s 97: a term "that would be unlawful under this Act is void". s 12(3)(c)(iii): every
-- statement "made in a document of another State or a Territory recognised as an advance care directive under section 95"
-- is a values directive (finding 2).
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `Interstate instrument`
      `it complies with the law of the place where it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how far` IS A `How far my instrument could have been made in Victoria`
GIVETH A `Whether my interstate instrument is recognised`
`ss 95-97 -- whether my interstate instrument is recognised` `the instrument` `it complies with the law of the place where it was made` `how far` MEANS
    IF `the instrument` EQUALS `an advance care directive made in another State or Territory`
    THEN BRANCH IF NOT `it complies with the law of the place where it was made`
                THEN `not recognised as a directive, but it may be considered as my preferences and values (s 95(2))`
                IF `how far` EQUALS `everything in it could validly have been given under this Act`
                THEN `recognised: taken to be an advance care directive under this Act, but its statements are values directives (ss 95(1), 12(3)(c)(iii))`
                IF `how far` EQUALS `only part of it could validly have been given under this Act`
                THEN `recognised in part, to the extent it could have been given under this Act; its statements are values directives (ss 95(1), 12(3)(c)(iii), 97)`
                OTHERWISE `not recognised as a directive, but it may be considered as my preferences and values (s 95(2))`
    ELSE BRANCH IF NOT `it complies with the law of the place where it was made`
                THEN `not covered: s 96 recognises it only if it complies with the law where it was made and to the extent Part 3 allows`
                IF `how far` EQUALS `everything in it could validly have been given under this Act`
                THEN `recognised: taken to be an appointment under Part 3 (s 96(1))`
                IF `how far` EQUALS `only part of it could validly have been given under this Act`
                THEN `recognised in part, to the extent the powers could have been given under Part 3 (ss 96(1), 97)`
                OTHERWISE `not covered: s 96 recognises it only if it complies with the law where it was made and to the extent Part 3 allows`

§§ `Offences that protect me (ss 14, 15, 41, 42, 84, 85)`

DECLARE `Offence against me` IS ONE OF
    `inducing me to give an advance care directive by dishonesty or undue influence (s 14(1))`
    `knowingly making a false or misleading statement about my directive or my attempt to give one (s 15)`
    `purporting to act as my appointed decision maker or support person without being one (s 41)`
    `inducing me to appoint a decision maker by dishonesty or undue influence (s 42(1))`
    `giving me a research procedure in an unapproved project (s 84)`
    `giving me a research procedure without consent or authorisation (s 85)`

DECLARE `Kind of offender` IS ONE OF
    `a natural person`
    `a body corporate`

DECLARE `Maximum penalty` HAS
    `penalty units` IS A NUMBER
    `years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER

-- ss 14(1), 15(1), (2), 42(1): "600 penalty units or imprisonment for 5 years or both in the case of a natural person;
-- 2400 penalty units in the case of a body corporate." s 41(1), (2): "600 penalty units or imprisonment for 5 years or
-- both" (no separate body corporate figure: fork F9, the same figures given; imprisonment cannot be imposed on a body
-- corporate). s 84: "240 penalty units." s 85: "240 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years or both." The value of a
-- penalty unit is set under the Monetary Units Act 2004, not deposited: the answer is in penalty units. 0 years: no
-- imprisonment.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence against me`
      `the offender` IS A `Kind of offender`
GIVETH A `Maximum penalty`
`the maximum penalty` `the offence` `the offender` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `purporting to act as my appointed decision maker or support person without being one (s 41)` THEN `Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 600, `years of imprisonment` IS 5
    WHEN `giving me a research procedure in an unapproved project (s 84)` THEN `Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 240, `years of imprisonment` IS 0
    WHEN `giving me a research procedure without consent or authorisation (s 85)` THEN `Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 240, `years of imprisonment` IS 2
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the offender` EQUALS `a body corporate`
        THEN `Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 2400, `years of imprisonment` IS 0
        ELSE `Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 600, `years of imprisonment` IS 5
